<LayoutPage title="Foldster's Projects — Dizzy's OBS Overlays" description="Custom stream overlays">
  <h1>Dizzy's OBS Overlays</h1>
  <p class="mono">for Dizzy</p>
  <p class="lede">
    A custom stream overlay package &mdash; plus a pipeline to push new scenes straight to her setup &mdash; the close-collaboration build, designed for a partner who streams a different vibe entirely from Bizzlebeard or Rewkers.
  </p>

  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Dizzy's stream has a softer, slower-paced aesthetic &mdash; crochet, conversation, walking the audience through her week. Generic high-contrast streaming overlays aren't right; she needed something that matches the warmth of the show.
  </p>

  <h2>What's Being Built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Custom overlay set in her color palette + type</li>
    <li>Subtle alerts (no jump-scare goblin sounds)</li>
    <li>Donation/follow recognition that's warm, not loud</li>
    <li>Day-of-the-week schedule strip</li>
    <li>Reusable across her platforms</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Shipping New Scenes Remotely</h2>
  <p>
    Beyond the overlays themselves, the setup is built so new scenes can be delivered to her without a screen-share session. Scenes are edited off-site in OBS, committed to git, and her one-click launcher pulls the latest, translates the asset paths from macOS to Windows, and opens OBS ready to stream.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Git-versioned scene collection &mdash; a WIP branch plus a ship-when-ready <code>deploy</code> branch her launcher tracks</li>
    <li>Cross-platform path translation (macOS &rarr; Windows) so scenes built on my machine just work on hers</li>
    <li>Git LFS for media assets &mdash; images, video, audio, browser sources, fonts</li>
    <li>One-click launcher: pull &rarr; translate &rarr; open OBS, with instant rollback to any prior version</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>
    Work in progress. Targeting late summer 2026 for completion ahead of Foldster's Projects' formal launch.
  </p>

  <p class="mono note">case study photos + demo clip + Dizzy quote coming when launched.</p>

  <a href="/contact/" class="cta" slot="cta">Want a custom overlay package &mdash; or a pipeline to push scene updates straight to your setup? &rarr;</a>
</LayoutPage>

